  "body": "I'm going through the incoming references to Selectors and I had a question: why does HTML [specify](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#selectors) that CSS's syntax is lowercased, HTML's tag/attribute name is lowercased, and then a case-sensitive match is performed rather than simply saying that HTML's attribute/tag names are considered [ASCII case-insensitive](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive)? (From my perspective it's really weird for the HTML spec to be manipulating CSS/Selectors syntax rather than merely classifying HTML things as case-sensitive or ASCII case-insensitive.)",
